---
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Quote from '../components/Quote.astro';
import ten from '../noalibi/Jun_22_2026_23_38_02.jpg';
---

<Page title="Testimonials" bodyClass="testimonials">
  <Quote cite="SSgt USAF">
    When I wanted to apply for SSDI after being released from the service, Barbi
    was outstanding. I can honestly state that the filing procedure would have
    been far more challenging and frustrating without her assistance. The last
    thing you want when you already have major health problems is to have to
    cope with the additional stress of navigating the Social Security system by
    yourself. Throughout the entire procedure, <strong
      >Barbi was sympathetic, understanding, and caring</strong
    >. She took the time to fully explain everything, respond to my inquiries,
    and provide me with constant assistance. Years later, I still employ her
    services for my SSDI reviews every three years, and I still think highly of
    her commitment and skill. She constantly goes above and beyond to assist her
    clients. <strong
      >I heartily suggest Barbi to anyone in need of help with Social Security
      or SSDI</strong
    > issues. Her expertise, compassion, and dedication to serving others are invaluable.
  </Quote>

  <Quote cite="Retired Captain USAF">
    <p>
      During my medical retirement process; I was enrolled into the Air Force
      Wounded Warrior Program for assistance. Through this enrollment I was
      contacted by Mrs. Barbi Law to assist me in filing a request for Social
      Security Disability Insurance (SSDI).
    </p>
    <p>
      In my opinion, <strong>Mrs. Law is a subject matter expert</strong> regarding
      the process of applying for SSDI. She guided me through the time intensive process
      of gathering the required documents to support the claim of disability, filed
      the claim online, assisted me with forms the Social Security Administration
      sent to clarify the claim of disability and acted on my behalf as a liaison
      with the Social Security Administration to ensure <strong
        >all request were answered in a timely manner</strong
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Amidst many other responsibilities, Mrs. Law generously volunteers her
      time, knowledge, patience and guidance to the Wounded Warrior Program. She
      demonstrates a sincere devotion in assisting Wounded Warriors through the
      difficult process of requesting SSDI and it was a pleasure working with
      her.
    </p>
    <p>
      I did not want the opportunity to pass without expressing my appreciation
      to Mrs. Law for being <strong
        >instrumental in my being awarded monthly disability payments</strong
      >.
    </p>
    <p>With deep appreciation.</p>
  </Quote>

  <Quote cite="SSgt USAF">
    <p>
      In December I had brain surgery and my case manager recommended that I
      apply for social security and to contact Barbi Law.
    </p>
    <p>
      My husband and I had a few meetings with her and she was nothing but      <strong>extremely friendly and helpful</strong>. She would contact the
      (SSA) administration on behalf of me in order to assist with my claim for
      social security benefits. She is very organized and made everything very
      easy by using different stickies and such.
    </p>
    <p>
      It turned out that I was not able to get social security because I did not
      meet the criteria, however, I am still glad that I tried because I got to
      meet Barbi and she is one of the nicest people that I have ever met. She
      is a God sent and my husband and I appreciate everything that she had
      done.
    </p>
  </Quote>

  <Quote cite="Retired SMSgt USAF">
    <p>
      My wife and I found you to be so <strong
        >understanding and compassionate</strong
      >. With a thorough understanding of the Disability system! The best part
      was when we had our phone consults we almost felt like it was face to face
      and you made that time completely dedicated to us without rushing. I know
      my wife appreciated your understanding of this being something we are both
      going through and I appreciated you allowing her to be my voice at times.
      You were amazing at taking the time to help us understand and we can not
      thank you enough for your kindness and time!!! You are truly a blessing!!!
      Thank you!!!
    </p>
  </Quote>

  <Quote cite="Medically Retired TSGT, USAF">
    <p>
      When I was going through the medical retirement process from the Air
      Force, my wife and I did as much research as we could and were told that
      we should apply for SSDI because of my combat-related diagnoses and
      disorders. We were turned down within weeks of applying. Having lost all
      hope regarding the Social Security Disability Insurance claim we were at
      an Air Force Wounded Warrior CARE Event when we were instructed to contact
      Barbi Laws for her knowledge and unparalleled help regarding SSDI. We
      jumped at the chance to receive help. My wife contacted Barbi over the
      phone and she agreed to help us after listening to a thorough explanation
      of my disorders and I'm so thankful that she did. Not only did her
      knowledge and effervescent personality help us to navigate the rocky
      layout of the SSA, but she provided us an ear to voice complaints and
      concerns. We would highly recommend using IGNiTE GOD'S LITE, LLC when you
      are attempting to apply for SSDI as we could not be happier.
    </p>
  </Quote>
  <Photo src={ten} alt={ten} class="center" />
  <Card>
    <p>
      We are honored to support our community. You can view more verified
      stories and our A+ rating directly on our
      <a
        href="https://www.bbb.org/us/tx/schertz/profile/disability/ignite-gods-lite-llc-0825-1000171401"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">BBB Business Profile</a
      >.
    </p>
  </Card>
</Page>

<style is:global>
  main {
    row-gap: var(--space-l);
  }
</style>
